notes               = "Untitled in source. Two rhymed quatrains (پریشان است / جانان است / آنست، then دوست / نیکوست / آهوست) — the classical manner again, as in fire-water (123) and village-nights (133-134). The argument is the Sufi one: for a man going toward the beloved there is no wrong direction, and his footprints become a road for whoever comes after. Autumn is months 7-9 → +621 = 2006. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
draft               = true

===persian===

وقتی که درویشی پریشان است
چون در هوای وصل جانان است
در هر بیابانی که راهی نیست،
هرسو که پایش رفت رَه آنست.
پا را چوبگذاری به راهِ دوست
رفتارِ تو کاری خوش و نیکوست،
تو رفته‌ای و جای پاهایت
شاید که راهِ چشمهٔ آهوست...
پاییز ۱۳۸۵

===machine===

When a dervish is distracted,
being in the air of union with the beloved,
then in any wilderness where there is no road,
whichever way his foot went — that is the road.
Once you set foot on the friend's road
your going is a good and a lovely work;
you have gone, and the place of your feet
may be the road to the gazelle's spring...
Autumn 1385

===lantern===

When a dervish is distracted,
being in the air of union with the beloved,
then in any wilderness where there is no road
whichever way his foot went — that is the road.
Once you set your foot on the friend's road
your going is a good and a lovely work;
you have gone, and the place of your feet
may turn out to be the road to the gazelle's spring...

Autumn 1385

